B. The quotient's shell kernel as the image sum K_P(x, y) = (1/120) sum_g U_N((g x).y)
   N = 12: invariant under 2I in each argument to 0e+00; K_P(x, x) = m_N = 1 to 3e-15; K_P(x, g x) = m_N at all 120 images to 6e-15
   N = 20: invariant under 2I in each argument to 1e-16; K_P(x, x) = m_N = 1 to 4e-16; K_P(x, g x) = m_N at all 120 images to 1e-14
   N = 30: invariant under 2I in each argument to 1e-16; K_P(x, x) = m_N = 1 to 2e-14; K_P(x, g x) = m_N at all 120 images to 4e-15

C. K_P(1, exp(eps n)) as a function of the direction n, eps = 0.3 rad; degrees l <= 30 carrying A5 invariants: [0, 6, 10, 12, 15, 16, 18, 20, 21, 22, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 30]
   N = 12: central part isotropic (its direction-dependent rms 6e-14 of its mean); non-central part carries l = [0, 6, 10, 12], all among the A5-invariant degrees: True; its direction-dependent rms 2.70e-02 of the variance m_N; invariant under the 60 rotations to 4e-16
   N = 20: central part isotropic (its direction-dependent rms 6e-14 of its mean); non-central part carries l = [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20], all among the A5-invariant degrees: True; its direction-dependent rms 1.46e-01 of the variance m_N; invariant under the 60 rotations to 1e-15
   N = 30: central part isotropic (its direction-dependent rms 6e-14 of its mean); non-central part carries l = [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24, 26], all among the A5-invariant degrees: True; its direction-dependent rms 1.27e-01 of the variance m_N; invariant under the 60 rotations to 1e-15

D. Three homogeneous laws on the cover's shell N (eps = 0.3 rad for the direction dependence)
   the nearest images of a point, at distance pi R/5, lie along the icosahedron's 12 vertex directions: True
   shell N = 12 (m_N = 1); nearest-image correlation baseline U_N(phi/2)/(N+1) = +0.1245
     A = I    : direction-dependent rms of the correlation 1.16e-14; invariant under the observer's 60 rotations to 0e+00, under a random rotation to 0e+00; nearest-image correlation +0.1245
     A = P    : direction-dependent rms of the correlation 2.70e-02; invariant under the observer's 60 rotations to 3e-16, under a random rotation to 7e-02; nearest-image correlation +1.0000
     A = I - P: direction-dependent rms of the correlation 2.25e-03; invariant under the observer's 60 rotations to 4e-16, under a random rotation to 7e-02; nearest-image correlation +0.0515
   shell N = 20 (m_N = 1); nearest-image correlation baseline U_N(phi/2)/(N+1) = +0.0476
     A = I    : direction-dependent rms of the correlation 1.76e-16; invariant under the observer's 60 rotations to 0e+00, under a random rotation to 0e+00; nearest-image correlation +0.0476
     A = P    : direction-dependent rms of the correlation 1.46e-01; invariant under the observer's 60 rotations to 9e-16, under a random rotation to 4e-01; nearest-image correlation +1.0000
     A = I - P: direction-dependent rms of the correlation 7.29e-03; invariant under the observer's 60 rotations to 9e-16, under a random rotation to 4e-01; nearest-image correlation -0.0000

E. The nine irreducible characters of 2I (1, 2, 2', 3, 3', 4, 4s, 5, 6; 4 is A5's, 4s the spinorial one, spin 3/2), dimensions [1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, 5, 6], squares summing to 120; orthonormal to 2e-16
   the first Sym^N with a repeated 2I constituent: N = 15; among even N: N = 16
   Sym^12: 1 + 3 + 4 + 5
   Sym^16: 3' + 4 + 2x5
   Sym^20: 1 + 3 + 3' + 4 + 2x5
   Sym^24: 1 + 3 + 3' + 2x4 + 2x5
   Sym^30: 1 + 2x3 + 2x3' + 2x4 + 2x5

F. Sym^N as unitary matrices, in which the quotient's kernel and every central law are image sums
   N = 12: a homomorphism to 1e-15, unitary to 1e-15, trace U_N(Re g) at all 120 to 6e-15; Tr(P rho_N(x y^-1)) = K_P(x, y) to 9e-16; a random central law equals its character-weighted image sum to 3e-15
      the whole-shell law weighted over its constituents: w = 51 at g = 1 and 51 at g = -1, at most 4.85 off the central pair; its kernel is U_N(x.y) to 2e-15, as it is with w = 120 at g = 1 alone
   N = 20: a homomorphism to 3e-15, unitary to 9e-16, trace U_N(Re g) at all 120 to 2e-14; Tr(P rho_N(x y^-1)) = K_P(x, y) to 8e-16; a random central law equals its character-weighted image sum to 1e-15
      the whole-shell law weighted over its constituents: w = 60 at g = 1 and 60 at g = -1, at most 0.00 off the central pair; its kernel is U_N(x.y) to 7e-16, as it is with w = 120 at g = 1 alone
   N = 30: a homomorphism to 3e-15, unitary to 2e-15, trace U_N(Re g) at all 120 to 2e-14; Tr(P rho_N(x y^-1)) = K_P(x, y) to 2e-15; a random central law equals its character-weighted image sum to 7e-15
      the whole-shell law weighted over its constituents: w = 60 at g = 1 and 60 at g = -1, at most 0.00 off the central pair; its kernel is U_N(x.y) to 4e-16, as it is with w = 120 at g = 1 alone

G. The laws on the cover's shell N with the observer's A5: the commutant of rho_N(2I)
   dimension = sum of squared multiplicities = number of A5-invariant harmonics of degree <= N (N = 0 to 60): True; real kernels, sum of m(m+1)/2 = number of even-degree ones (even N): True
   N = 12: the average over 2I is a projector to 1e-16 of rank 4 (squared multiplicities sum to 4; invariant degrees [0, 6, 10, 12]); the center has dimension 4
   N = 20: the average over 2I is a projector to 2e-16 of rank 8 (squared multiplicities sum to 8; invariant degrees [0, 6, 10, 12, 15, 16, 18, 20]); the center has dimension 5
   N = 24: the average over 2I is a projector to 2e-16 of rank 11 (squared multiplicities sum to 11; invariant degrees [0, 6, 10, 12, 15, 16, 18, 20, 21, 22, 24]); the center has dimension 5
   N = 30: the average over 2I is a projector to 3e-16 of rank 17 (squared multiplicities sum to 17; invariant degrees [0, 6, 10, 12, 15, 16, 18, 20, 21, 22, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 30]); the center has dimension 5

H. The center: image correlations at the isotropic baseline at every g only when A is a multiple of I
   N = 12: the 4 constituent characters are independent on 2I (smallest singular value 10.95); equal weights give the baseline to 5e-16; 100 random weightings in [0.2, 1] miss it by at least 0.0135
   N = 20: the 5 constituent characters are independent on 2I (smallest singular value 10.95); equal weights give the baseline to 1e-15; 100 random weightings in [0.2, 1] miss it by at least 0.0083
   N = 24: the 5 constituent characters are independent on 2I (smallest singular value 10.95); equal weights give the baseline to 6e-16; 100 random weightings in [0.2, 1] miss it by at least 0.0165
   N = 30: the 5 constituent characters are independent on 2I (smallest singular value 10.95); equal weights give the baseline to 8e-16; 100 random weightings in [0.2, 1] miss it by at least 0.0135

I. Outside the center: A5 anisotropy with every image correlation unchanged (eps = 0.3 rad)
   N = 12: the non-central part is 1e-15 of the averaged matrix: here the commutant is its center
   N = 20: non-central part 0.30 of the averaged matrix; with it scaled to unit norm as T, max |Tr(T rho(g))| over 2I 5e-14, [T, rho(g)] 7e-15, [T, rho(h)] for a random h 0.46
      A = I + T/2: smallest eigenvalue 0.50; kernel real to 5e-15; image correlations minus baseline 1e-15; direction-dependent rms of the correlation 1.04e-02, in degrees [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18], all even and A5-invariant: True
   N = 24: non-central part 0.33 of the averaged matrix; with it scaled to unit norm as T, max |Tr(T rho(g))| over 2I 2e-14, [T, rho(g)] 7e-15, [T, rho(h)] for a random h 0.64
      A = I + T/2: smallest eigenvalue 0.50; kernel real to 8e-15; image correlations minus baseline 6e-16; direction-dependent rms of the correlation 3.72e-02, in degrees [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20], all even and A5-invariant: True
   N = 30: non-central part 0.60 of the averaged matrix; with it scaled to unit norm as T, max |Tr(T rho(g))| over 2I 3e-14, [T, rho(g)] 6e-15, [T, rho(h)] for a random h 0.47
      A = I + T/2: smallest eigenvalue 0.50; kernel real to 9e-15; image correlations minus baseline 4e-16; direction-dependent rms of the correlation 2.08e-02, in degrees [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24], all even and A5-invariant: True

J. What the image correlations see: the constituent weights alone, averaging chi_rho(g)/d_rho
   N = 12: for each single-constituent law and 20 random A5 laws, the image correlations equal the average of chi_rho(g)/d_rho weighted by Tr(P_rho A), to 2e-15; at the nearest images the family spans [-0.2500, +1.0000], with P2 at +1.0000 and the baseline at +0.1245
   N = 20: for each single-constituent law and 20 random A5 laws, the image correlations equal the average of chi_rho(g)/d_rho weighted by Tr(P_rho A), to 5e-15; at the nearest images the family spans [-0.2500, +1.0000], with P2 at +1.0000 and the baseline at +0.0476
   N = 24: for each single-constituent law and 20 random A5 laws, the image correlations equal the average of chi_rho(g)/d_rho weighted by Tr(P_rho A), to 3e-15; at the nearest images the family spans [-0.2500, +1.0000], with P2 at +1.0000 and the baseline at +0.0000
   N = 30: for each single-constituent law and 20 random A5 laws, the image correlations equal the average of chi_rho(g)/d_rho weighted by Tr(P_rho A), to 3e-15; at the nearest images the family spans [-0.2500, +1.0000], with P2 at +1.0000 and the baseline at +0.0323
